# Vercel — explicit ignore list for the `sites/lund-podiatry` subdirectory deploy.
#
# When Vercel's "Root Directory" setting is `sites/lund-podiatry`, Vercel reads
# this file just like .gitignore to decide which files within that subdirectory
# are NOT included in the build input / production CDN bundle.
#
# Keep this file minimal. Only list things we explicitly do not want shipped.
# Patterns follow .gitignore syntax (with one Vercel-specific extra: ! negation).
#
# Reference: https://vercel.com/docs/projects/vercelignore

# --- OS + editor junk (defensive — Vercel already strips most of these for HTTP cleanliness)
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.bak
*.tmp
*~

# --- Local-only framework artifacts (defensive — Vercel does not deploy node_modules anyway)
node_modules/
.vercel/
.turbo/
.next/

# --- Dev-only scripts / tests (kept in repo for engineering convenience, never shipped to CDN)
tests/
__tests__/
test/
spec/
*.test.mjs
*.test.ts
*.spec.ts

# --- These are not needed in the deploy input because Vercel does NOT run an
# install or build step for this static site (Build/Install/Output commands all empty).
package.json
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# --- Internal documentation (live in repo for engineering handoff; intentionally NOT shipped)
# README.md is intentionally shipped — informs the team without exposing sensitive info.
# If you ever add a STRATEGY.md or other internal-only doc, list it here.
# STRATEGY.md
# CHANGELOG.md
# TODO.md
